{# ===========================================================================
   Component: location-menu

   Section 4 of the location page template in SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md: "menu
   section for this location, from menu.json filtered by `locations`. Link to
   /menu/."

   USAGE
     {% set menuLoc = loc.id %}
     {% include "components/location-menu.njk" %}

   Optional: `menuTitle` (safe HTML), `menuNote` (safe HTML), `menuTitleId`.

   WHY IT READS AS A MENU AND NOT A LIST OF NAMES.

   The rows are grouped under the same three sections the menu page uses, in
   the same order, and each heading links into that section's anchor on
   /menu/. That grouping is what makes eleven names parse as a menu rather
   than as a run of words, and the anchors mean "see the whole menu" lands on
   the part the reader was already reading.

   NO DESCRIPTIONS, AND THIS WAS MEASURED. The first build of this component
   printed each dish's description under its name. It read better on any one
   page and was a regression across five. The descriptions are identical in
   every room, so carrying them raised the worst pairwise sentence overlap
   between the five stub pages to 0.438 and Maui's shared-text share to 57 per
   cent, against 0.424 and 59 before this section existed at all. Dropping
   them lands at 0.368 and 49, which is the point of adding the section.
   These are the pages that are noindexed today precisely because they read as
   each other, so 200 words of identical dish copy on a 400 word page is the
   opposite of the fix. Descriptions live on /menu/, which is one page and can
   carry them, and on /tajima-convoy/, under that room's own photographs,
   where they appear once.

   NO PRICES, and this is not an oversight. menu.json `_priceStatus` records
   that the brand prices are stale against the live catalogs, that Plaza
   Bonita runs about two dollars under the other San Diego rooms and Maui runs
   above them, and therefore that no single price is right for all seven. A
   per-location menu is the one surface where printing a brand price would be
   most obviously wrong. /menu/ prints them; this does not.

   Availability comes from `dish.locations`, which was derived from the seven
   live Toast catalogs by exact name match (menu.json `_availabilityStatus`),
   not assumed. That is why Plaza Bonita shows seven rows and Convoy eleven.

   Descriptions are menu.json's own and carry its DRAFT PENDING CLIENT
   APPROVAL status, the same status they already ship under on /menu/. A dish
   with no description renders without one rather than getting a written one.
   =========================================================================== #}
{%- set mId = menuTitleId | default("menu-title") %}
{%- set sections = [
  { key: "ramen",   label: "Ramen",        anchor: "/menu/#ramen" },
  { key: "izakaya", label: "Small plates", anchor: "/menu/#izakaya" },
  { key: "dessert", label: "To finish",    anchor: "/menu/#dessert" }
] %}
<section class="sect" aria-labelledby="{{ mId }}">
  <div class="sect__inner">
    <header class="sect__head">
      <span class="mark mark--lg mark--disc sect__mark" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#i-ramen-bowl"></use></svg></span>
      <h2 class="sect__title" id="{{ mId }}">{{ menuTitle | default("What comes out of <em>this room.</em>") | safe }}</h2>
      {%- if menuNote %}
      <p class="sect__note">{{ menuNote | safe }}</p>
      {%- endif %}
    </header>

    {%- for section in sections %}
      {%- set rows = menu.items | dishesFor(menuLoc, section.key) %}
      {%- if rows | length %}
    <div class="here-group">
      <h3 class="here-group__title">
        <a class="here-group__link" href="{{ section.anchor }}">{{ section.label }}</a>
      </h3>
      <ul class="here-list">
        {%- for dish in rows %}
        <li class="here-list__item">
          <p class="here-list__head">
            <span class="here-list__name">{{ dish.name }}</span>
            {%- if dish.romaji %}<span class="here-list__romaji">{{ dish.romaji }}</span>{% endif %}
          </p>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
      {%- endif %}
    {%- endfor %}

    {#- The full menu and this room's printable one, under the list they
        belong to rather than stranded in the section note. -#}
    {%- set menuLinksLoc = menuLoc %}
    {% include "components/menu-links.njk" %}
  </div>
</section>
